You are a code reviewer. Working directory: /tmp/hzt-3388928427/bench-run-dfitdwgy/clone/.harness/worktrees/orch-VocanicZ_bench-run-20261115-medium-harness-opus-harness-opus-r05-p1 (a git worktree; do not cd elsewhere, do not modify repo files, do not commit). Put any scratch files under a fresh mktemp -d directory.

Task: verify the Python package `stockroom` (src/stockroom/, tests/) against the spec. Spec = `brief.md` in the repo (top authority) plus PRD issue #1 (read with `gh issue view 1 -R VocanicZ/bench-run-20261115-medium-harness-opus-harness-opus-r05 --json body`); its `## Acceptance criteria` and `## Implementation Decisions` sections matter. Where brief and PRD conflict, brief wins.

1. For EVERY acceptance criterion in the PRD, state MET / UNMET with evidence (exact command/call and observed output). Check correctness and edge cases: pricing math (half-up rounding, 5%/10% volume discount thresholds, 3% order discount at exactly 500.00, penny allocation floor+largest remainder with earliest-line tie break, per-line tax, no -0.00), fulfil's "lowest later balance" rule and previous shipments, invoice, report sorting/format (text/csv/json), exit codes 0/1/2 and order of checks (command line → read files → parse → request), file left byte-for-byte unchanged on refusal, newline-append behavior, commands only reading the files they need, `--dir` anywhere, both `--dir DIR` and `--dir=DIR`. Also verify `pip install .` into a temp venv gives `import stockroom` and a working `stockroom` command (use `python3 -m venv` in a temp dir).

2. ROBUSTNESS PROBE — run ALL of these against the real CLI (python -m stockroom or the installed script) with temp data dirs, and report every result PASS or FAIL with the exact command:
 - a value starting with a dash as positional (e.g. `stockroom history -x`, `stockroom ship 2024-03-10 AB-100 -3`, `stockroom receive 2024-03-10 AB-100 5 -note`, `stockroom quote -`) and as an option value (`--dir -x`, `--dir -`, `--format -x`, `--dir` with no value);
 - output piped into `head -1` (`stockroom stock | head -1` with many products, also `report`, `history`, `--json`): no traceback/error on stderr, exit 0 (check PIPESTATUS);
 - a UTF-8 BOM at start of each of the three files;
 - CRLF and lone-CR line endings (lone CR must NOT end a line — so it's part of the field, likely a mistake or kept in note);
 - a form feed (U+000C) and U+2028 inside a field (name, note, customer) — must not split lines; check how output shows them;
 - non-ASCII digits in numbers, empty files, a huge file (e.g. 100k movements) for performance, non-UTF-8 bytes (exit 2), missing dir (exit 2), --dir pointing at a file.

3. Report also any user-visible I/O issues you notice (argument handling, error messages, output format, exit status, encodings) even if minor — list each as a separate finding with a reproduction command and expected vs actual.

Be terse in the final report: criteria table (MET/UNMET + evidence), probe results list (PASS/FAIL + command), findings list (each: repro, expected, actual, severity). Do not pad.

